# The enforcement surface. Replace @OWNER with a real human owner and enable
# "Require review from Code Owners" on the protected branch; that host
# setting is what makes AGENTS.md's "loosening requires human countersign"
# mechanical instead of advisory. pyproject.toml, ruff.toml, and
# pyrightconfig.json are unanchored on purpose: Ruff resolves the nearest
# config and pyrightconfig.json outranks pyproject.toml, so a nested or root
# copy shadows the wall; .basedpyright/ holds baselines that silence
# pre-existing errors. If the mise task fragment (20-python.toml) lives
# outside /.config/mise/, add its path here.
.basedpyright/ @OWNER
.ruff.toml @OWNER
/.config/mise/ @OWNER
/.github/ @OWNER
/.mutmut-floor @OWNER
/AGENTS.md @OWNER
